3. The patient's history of ITP is at least 3 months (persistent or chronic ITP);
4. The platelet count of the subject within 24 hours before the first administration of the study drug is less than 30 × 10\^9/L; during the screening period, platelet count is measured at least twice (at least 1 week apart), with an average platelet count of less than 30 × 10\^9/L and no platelet count greater than 35 × 10\^9/L;
5. First line treatment, such as ineffective hormone or immunoglobulin therapy, or ITP patients who relapse after treatment;
